.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt AUTOMENU 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm automenu
.Nd text menu in the style of the Auto-Menu systems of the 1980s
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar file
.Nm
.Fl \-kiosk
.Op Ar file
.Nm
.Fl \-hash
.Op Ar name
.Nm
.Fl \-check
.Op Ar file
.Nm
.Fl \-version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows a menu that is read from a text file.
A key press opens a submenu, shows a text or runs a command.
.Pp
Use: arrow keys and Enter, the digits 1 to 9 select an item directly,
a mouse click runs an item, the mouse wheel selects,
Esc or Backspace go back one menu, Ctrl-C quits the program.
.Pp
Without
.Ar file
the first existing file from the list under
.Sx FILES
is used.
.Pp
With
.Fl \-kiosk
Ctrl-C does not quit the program.
The way out remains an
.Cm exit
item, which can be locked with a password.
.Pp
With
.Fl \-check
the file is only checked.
Errors are reported with the line number.
.Pp
With
.Fl \-hash
.Op Ar name
a password is asked for twice (no echo) and the matching
.Cm password
line for the menu file is printed.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl \-kiosk
Kiosk mode: Ctrl-C does not quit the program.
.It Fl \-check
Only check the file, do not start the menu.
.It Fl \-hash Op Ar name
Create a password line, without a name
.Dq admin .
.It Fl \-version
Print the version number.
.El
.Pp
At most one option may stand before the file.
.Sh PASSWORDS
Single items can be locked with a password.
First create the line:
.Pp
.Dl automenu \-\-hash admin
.Pp
The printed
.Cm password
line belongs into the menu file, and the item gets
.Cm lock admin
before its type.
The name is freely chosen and has nothing to do with user accounts.
Only a hash is stored (PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256, 20000 rounds, random salt).
.Pp
The password is asked again on every selection of a locked item.
After a wrong password there is a wait of 1 second,
after 3 failed attempts the menu is shown again after a wait of 3 seconds.
A whole menu cannot be locked, only the item that leads to it.
A forgotten password is replaced by replacing the
.Cm password
line in the file with a new one.
.Sh SECURITY
The password lock and the option
.Fl \-kiosk
are a lock against the curious and against mistakes, not a security feature.
Whoever can read the menu file can run the commands directly in the shell.
In normal mode Ctrl-C quits the program without a password.
.Fl \-kiosk
locks only Ctrl-C.
Closing the window, SSH or a second shell remain possible,
and programs with a shell function such as
.Xr vi 1
or
.Xr top 1
lead out of the menu.
The menu file should be owned by the user and readable only by that user
.Pq Ql chmod 600 .
Where real security is needed, the user rights of the system are responsible.
.Sh FILES
Search order:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/automenu/menu.mdf
.It Pa ~/.config/automenu/menu.mdf
.It Pa PREFIX/etc/automenu/menu.mdf
System-wide default.
In each folder
.Pa menu.mdf
is searched first, then
.Pa menu.txt .
.It Pa PREFIX/etc/automenu/menu.mdf.sample
Example, installed with the program.
.It Pa PREFIX/share/examples/automenu/
More examples.
.El
.Sh FILE FORMAT
One line per entry.
Empty lines and lines starting with
.Ql #
are ignored.
The first menu in the file is the start menu.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm menu Ar id Qq Title
Starts a new menu.
.It Cm item Qq Text Cm run Ar command
Runs the command with
.Xr sh 1 .
.It Cm item Qq Text Cm menu Ar id
Opens another menu.
.It Cm item Qq Text Cm info Op Ar text
Shows a text.
.It Cm item Qq Text Cm back
Goes back.
.It Cm item Qq Text Cm exit
Quits the program.
.It Cm item Qq Text Op Qq Help text Cm lock Ar name ...
Locks the item: before it is run the password
.Ar name
is asked for, every time.
After 3 failed attempts the menu is shown again.
.It Cm password Ar name Ar hash
Defines a password (create the hash with
.Fl \-hash ) .
.It Cm set blackout Ar seconds
Blank the screen after this time without input, 0 = off.
.It Cm set clock Ar utc|local
Clock in UTC or local time.
.It Cm set mouse Ar on|off
Mouse on or off, default on.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Location of the user configuration, default
.Pa ~/.config .
.It Ev NO_COLOR
If set: no colours, inverse video only.
.It Ev AUTOMENU_COLORS
.Ql 256 ,
.Ql 16
or
.Ql mono
forces the colour depth.
.It Ev AUTOMENU_FRAME
.Ql solid
(default, coloured areas),
.Ql lines
(double lines, needs a font with line characters) or
.Ql ascii .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
menu start "My menu"
  item "Date"   run date
  item "Quit"   exit
.Ed
.Sh HISTORY
The idea comes from
.Em Automenu
by Marshall W. Magee and Magee Enterprises, Inc. (Norcross, Georgia, USA).
The program appeared from 1983 for MS-DOS as shareware and made it possible
to start programs and commands with a single key press
using a menu definition file (MDF, Menu Definition File).
It was fast, easy to use and a brilliant solution for countless users all over the world.
Today it is no longer sold and can only be found in archives.
.Pp
This
.Nm
is an independent new implementation in C for macOS, Linux and FreeBSD,
and later for the ESP32.
It contains no code of the original.
The menu definition file and the look deliberately recall the original.
.Pp
The name Automenu is a homage to the original.
This project has no connection to Magee Enterprises, Inc.
